    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0502" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Four Power Pact/18: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-03-31T18:00:00-05:00">March 31, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. For Davis. Your 62, March 31, 3 p.m. The Italian Ambassador<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d294-f1"/> has left with me a brief résumé of the proposed
                        agreement.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d294-f2"/>
                    <pb facs="0503" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>, under London date line today,
                    carries purported full text from “trustworthy source”. Article 4 contains
                    references to Colonial cooperation not mentioned in Italian Embassy’s outline.
                    Unless you can ascertain that the <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi> story is
                    substantially accurate, please cable full text as given by Grandi.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
